    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d340">

                <pb facs="0804" n="720" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg720"/>

                <head>No. 336.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Jackson to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-08-28"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 28, 1886</date>.
                        (Received September 7.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 303.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith what
                    purports to be a semiofficial Mexican statement of the Erresuris case.</p>
                <p>The <hi rendition="#italic">El Siglo XIX</hi> is the evening official paper of
                    the Mexican Government</p>
                <pb facs="0805" n="721" xml:id="pg721"/>
                <p>I have thought it wise to send it in connection with my dispatch No. 301 of
                    yesterday.</p>
                <p>I will also send a copy to Consul Linn for his information.</p>
                <p>I am. &amp;c.</p>
                <closer><signed>HENRY R. JACKSON.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d340-a1.xml" xpointer="d340-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
